{"kind":"turn","case_id":"ru01","request_sha":"7f6b5bdd954df163","outcome":{"text":"**Executive Summary:**\nThe mean Normalized Difference Vegetation Index (NDVI) for this 11.13 km² area is 0.42[[r_3fa9c2d41b7e08aa#mean]], measured from the Sentinel-2 acquisition on 2026-09-20. This level of greenness is characteristic of moderate vegetation density, such as mixed urban greenery, grassland, or sparse canopy cover.\n\n**Spatial Statistics:**\n- **Mean NDVI:** 0.42[[r_3fa9c2d41b7e08aa#mean]]\n- **Clear Pixel Coverage:** 96.1%[[r_3fa9c2d41b7e08aa#valid_pixel_pct]] valid cloud-masked pixels within the AOI\n\n**Anomalies & Patterns:**\nThe observation had high data quality, with 96.1%[[r_3fa9c2d41b7e08aa#valid_pixel_pct]] of pixels unobstructed by cloud or cloud shadow. A regional mean NDVI of 0.42[[r_3fa9c2d41b7e08aa#mean]] indicates substantial heterogeneity, typically pointing to an environment intermixed with non-vegetated surfaces (such as roads, bare soil, or structures) and vegetated pockets.\n\n**Follow-up Suggestions:**\n1. Would you like to examine the built-up surface fraction using ESA WorldCover to see the balance of urban infrastructure versus vegetation?\n2. Would you like to run anomaly detection to determine whether this September 2026 NDVI value is typical compared to the multi-year baseline for this area?","toolCalls":[],"finishReason":"stop"},"latency_ms":13169}
